.TH KAGI-VOLUME-ATTACH 1 "November 2026" "Kagi 0.39.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kagi-volume-attach \- connect a Kagi NBD export to a Linux block device
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B scripts/kagi-volume-attach
.I HOST[:PORT] /dev/nbdN
.RI [ BLOCK-SIZE ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Connects a running Kagi NBD frontend to the selected Linux NBD device using
.BR nbd-client .
The default port is 10809 and the default client block size is 4096 bytes.
The helper requests the compatibility export name
.BR keyspace .
.PP
The helper attempts to load the
.B nbd
kernel module.
Run it with permission to configure the chosen device, and use an unused
NBD device.
Before disconnecting, stop I/O and unmount any filesystem on the device.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
sudo scripts/kagi-volume-attach 127.0.0.1:10809 /dev/nbd0
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kagi-volume-nbd (1),
.BR kagi-volume-iscsi-export (1),
.BR nbd-client (8)
